<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 21 October, from 1094 to 1966.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/el-cid.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1094">1094 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">932 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">El Cid routs an Almoravid army at the Battle of Cuarte</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Months after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid">El Cid</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, an Almoravid army under Muhammad ibn Tashfin, sent to recover the city, camped on the plain of Cuarte. El Cid sallied out and routed it, the first major defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cuarte">Battle of Cuarte</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid">El Cid</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1096">1096 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">930 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Seljuk Turks destroy the People's Crusade at Civetot</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The undisciplined People's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a>, inspired by Peter the Hermit, was ambushed and annihilated by Seljuk forces near Civetot in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. On its way east, the movement had massacred Jewish communities in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1097">1097 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">929 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The First Crusade reaches Antioch and begins its siege</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A day after forcing the Iron Bridge over the Orontes, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a> reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemond-i-of-antioch">Bohemond of Taranto</a> leading the vanguard. Bohemond, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-iv-of-toulouse">Raymond IV of Toulouse</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/godfrey-of-bouillon">Godfrey of Bouillon</a> took positions at different gates for a siege of nine months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemond-i-of-antioch">Bohemond I of Antioch</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/godfrey-of-bouillon">Godfrey of Bouillon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-iv-of-toulouse">Raymond IV of Toulouse</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1345">1345 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">681 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Earl of Derby defeats a larger French army at Auberoche</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the Gascon campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>, an Anglo-Gascon force of 1,200 under Henry, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/earl-of-derby">Earl of Derby</a>, heavily defeated a French army of 7,000 under Louis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> at Auberoche, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perigueux">Périgueux</a>. The French leaders were killed or captured.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1600">1600 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">426 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tokugawa Ieyasu wins the Battle of Sekigahara</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> defeated a coalition of western lords at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a>, helped by defections mid-battle. The victory led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa shogunate</a>, which ruled a largely peaceful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> for more than 250 years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Battle of Sekigahara</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1805">1805 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">221 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nelson defeats the French and Spanish fleets at Trafalgar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a>'s fleet destroyed the combined French and Spanish fleets off Cape Trafalgar, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s hopes of invading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. Nelson was mortally wounded by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musket</a> ball during the battle.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1879">1879 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">147 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edison's carbon-filament lamp begins a 13-hour test</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Menlo Park, Thomas Edison's team lit a bulb with a carbonised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>-thread filament that glowed for about 13.5 hours. The result made long-lasting electric lighting practical.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1966">1966 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">60 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A colliery spoil tip engulfs a school at Aberfan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> waste tip slid down onto the Welsh village of Aberfan, burying Pantglas Junior School. The disaster killed 144 people, 116 of them children, and an inquiry blamed the National Coal Board.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 21 October <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alessandro-sforza"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alessandro-sforza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alessandro Sforza</span><span class="tp">1409–1473</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joachim-ernest-prince-of-anhalt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joachim-ernest-prince-of-anhalt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joachim Ernest, Prince of Anhalt</span><span class="tp">1536–1586</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/herman-willem-daendels"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/herman-willem-daendels.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Herman Willem Daendels</span><span class="tp">1762–1818</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alphonse-de-lamartine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alphonse-de-lamartine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alphonse de Lamartine</span><span class="tp">1790–1869</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfred-nobel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfred-nobel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfred Nobel</span><span class="tp">1833–1896</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
